.TH "libnvme_realloc" 9 "libnvme_realloc" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvme_realloc \- Resize an allocated memory buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void *" libnvme_realloc
.BI "(void *p "  ","
.BI "size_t len "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "p" 12
Existing memory buffer to resize
.IP "len" 12
New size in bytes
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Resizes the memory buffer referenced by \fIp\fP to \fIlen\fP bytes. The returned
buffer may be relocated. On successful expansion, any newly allocated
portion of the buffer is zero-initialized.

If \fIp\fP is NULL, this function behaves like \fBlibnvme_alloc\fP.
.SH "RETURN"
Pointer to the resized memory buffer on success, or NULL on failure.
On failure, the original buffer referenced by \fIp\fP remains valid and
unchanged.
